<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/idaho-falls.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/idaho-falls-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/idaho-falls.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/idaho-appraisal-areas/">Service areas</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Idaho Falls</span></nav><p class="kicker">Eastern Idaho</p><h1>Idaho Falls Insurance Appraiser</h1><p class="lede">Idaho Falls sits on the Upper Snake River Plain, where summer hail, strong wind and deep winter cold all take turns. Claims here often involve more than one peril on the same building.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line-w" href="/schedule-a-consult/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Bonneville County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Eastern Idaho</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="localbox"><div><h2 class="lb-t">Local claim risks</h2><ul class="chips"><li>Hail</li><li>High wind</li><li>Frozen pipes</li><li>Snow load</li><li>Ice dams</li></ul></div><div><h2 class="lb-t">Housing mix</h2><p>Older numbered-street homes, newer subdivisions in Ammon, commercial buildings</p></div></div>

<h2>Weather on the Upper Snake</h2>
<p>Idaho Falls winters are long and cold, and the open plain lets wind drive snow and cold air hard against buildings. Frozen pipes, ice dams and snow-load damage are common winter claims. Summer brings thunderstorms that can produce hail and damaging gusts across Bonneville, Bingham and Jefferson counties.</p>
<p>The city’s older neighborhoods near downtown and along the Snake River Greenbelt include homes from the early and mid-twentieth century. Newer subdivisions extend into Ammon and toward Iona and Ucon. Commercial and institutional buildings around the city serve a regional economy tied to agriculture and the Idaho National Laboratory.</p>
<h2>What an Idaho Falls insurance appraiser sees</h2>
<ul>
<li>Hail damage to roofs, siding and window screens after summer storms.</li>
<li>Wind damage to shingles, fences and outbuildings.</li>
<li>Frozen-pipe and ice-dam water losses during cold snaps.</li>
<li>Snow-load damage to carports, patio covers and agricultural buildings.</li>
<li>Commercial flat-roof claims on retail and office properties.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Serving Eastern Idaho</h2>
<p>We serve Idaho Falls, Ammon, Iona, Ucon, Shelley, Rigby and surrounding communities in Bonneville, Bingham and Jefferson counties.</p>

<h2>Services for Idaho Falls property owners</h2>
<p>Every Idaho Insurance Appraiser service is available in Idaho Falls and the surrounding area, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/appraisal-clause-appraiser/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/home-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/commercial-hoa-farm-appraisal/">Commercial, HOA &amp; Farm Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/wind-microburst-claim-appraisal/">Wind &amp; Microburst Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/water-frozen-pipe-appraisal/">Water &amp; Frozen Pipe Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-appraisal/wildfire-claim-appraisal/">Wildfire Claim Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions for a Idaho Falls Insurance Appraiser</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Hail and wind both hit my roof. Does that matter?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It can affect which deductible applies and how damage is documented. The appraisal itself focuses on the total amount of covered loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can ice-dam damage be appraised?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>If the insurer accepts coverage for the interior water damage and the dispute is over the cost of repair, yes.</p></div></details></div>
